      <activity id="ae7b46fa-dab0-54a8-b963-5948f94543fe" activityNameId="bda4970a-be80-553f-8570-61118b82695a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, low voltage, consumer, according to BFE 2005, at grid</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, low voltage, consumer, according to BFE 2005, at grid
This dataset describes the transmission of high voltage electricity.;
UUID: f47303fc-f50e-3237-82af-e96f079f4435
Included are the electricity production in Abbreviation, the transmission network and direct emissions to air (ozone and N2O). Electricity losses are accounted for.
Location: Data apply to public and self producers. Geographical classification according to IEA. Ozone- and NO2-emission factors are based on published measurements made in various countries.  Assumptions for transmission network, losses and emissions are based on Swiss data.
Technology: Average technology used to transmit and distribute electricity. Includes underground and overhead lines. Electricity production according to related datasets
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: production volume on low voltage level: 51'000GWh
Sampling: statistics 
Extrapolations: unknown electricity is modeled with UCTE-electricity mix
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f47303fc-f50e-3237-82af-e96f079f4435.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
